outputs:
Correct option: B. Causes a left-to-right shunt  

Rationale: After birth systemic arterial pressure exceeds pulmonary arterial pressure, so blood flows from the aorta through the ductus into the pulmonary artery—i.e., a left-to-right shunt.  
• Option A is only sometimes true (helpful in certain duct-dependent lesions, but usually not);  
• Option C is incorrect—PDA is in fact commonly associated with IVH, pulmonary hemorrhage and NEC in pre-term infants;  
• Option D is false—persistent patency at 14 days in a term infant is abnormal;  
• Option E is misleading—many close, but not all, and complications are well documented.

